  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "If $U={1,2,3,\u2026,10}$ is the universal set and $A={2,4,6,8,10},$ then the complement of $A$ is",
  "worked_solution": "The complement of $A,$ denoted $\\overset{\u2015}{A},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $A.$\n\nThe elements of $U$ that are not in $A$ are $1,$ $3,$ $5,$ $7,$ and $9.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{A}={1,3,5,7,9}.\n$$",
